      "id": "theverge-2026-06-27-the-17-best-robot-vacuum-deals-you-can-still-get-before-prim",
      "title": "The 17 best robot vacuum deals you can still get before Prime Day ends",
      "summary": "Our former top pick the Roborock S8 MaxV Ultra is now just $600, which is more than half its original price at launch. | Image: Roborock\t\n\nIf you’ve been wanting to buy a robot vacuum but have been put off by how much it can cost to get a good one, now is not a bad time to start looking. We’re now on the final day of Prime Day, and Amazon, along with retailers like Best Buy and Walmart, is still o",
      "body": "If you’ve been wanting to buy a robot vacuum but have been put off by how much it can cost to get a good one, now is not a bad time to start looking. We’re now on the final day of Prime Day, and Amazon, along with retailers like Best Buy and Walmart, is still offering discounts on several models we’ve tested from brands like Roborock, Dreame, and Shark. Whether you’re looking for a basic robot vacuum that can cut down on the amount of vacuuming you have to do or a high-end model that can wash and dry its own mop pads and climb over room thresholds, there are deals available across a wide range of price points.\n[Product: Roborock Saros 20 | https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.roborock.com%2Fproducts%2Froborock-saros-20]\n* The Roborock Q10 S5 Plus is down to $239.99 ($310 off), which is a new low price, at Amazon. The Q10 S5 Plus is one of our favorite budget-friendly robot vacuum / mop hybrids, combining good AI-powered obstacle avoidance with automatic carpet detection. It also features a vibrating mop that does a solid job scrubbing hard floors while lifting itself over rugs, and the set includes a self-emptying dock for added convenience. It can’t match the suction power or tall threshold-climbing abilities of pricier models like the Saros 20, but this is a good value under $300.\n[Product: Roborock Saros 10 | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Froborock-saros-10-ultra-thin-self-lifting-robot-vacuum-and-mop--22000-pa-suction-hyper-force-and-multi-fuction-dock-white%2FJJ8F5PCPP3%2Fsku%2F6615280%3Firclickid%3DUHRVuG0coxyZR9pwaD3LkU4CUkuTCyS1Q2yxU00%26irgwc%3D1%26afsrc%3D1%26ref%3D198%26loc%3DVox%2520Media%26acampID%3D%26mpid%3D482924%26affgroup%3D%2522Content%2522, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.roborock.com%2Fproducts%2Froborock-saros-10]\n* The Tapo RV30 Max Plus is another excellent budget-friendly option that’s on sale. It includes a self-emptying dock and costs $199.99 ($200 off) at Amazon. You don’t get AI-powered obstacle avoidance with this one, and its 5,200Pa suction isn’t the most powerful we’ve seen, but it’s still a capable cleaning machine with a wide mop pad that performs surprisingly well. The RV30 Max also offers excellent lidar-based navigation, support for room-specific cleaning, and Matter compatibility, allowing you to control it through all the major smart home platforms.\n[Product: Eufy Omni C28 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FWK41WF2?tag=theverge02-20, https://eufy-us.sjv.io/c/482924/999452/13094?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eufy.com%2Fproducts%2Ft211a110%3Fvariant%3D45573047124154]\n* Dreame’s X60 Max Ultra is on sale for $1,344.99 ($355 off) at Amazon and Dreame (with code X60UMCWS), which is its best price to date. We highly recommend the Dreame X60 Ultra for homes with lots of carpet, as it combines powerful 35,000Pa suction with dual rubber brushes that excel at lifting hair and debris. It can also climb over tall thresholds and thick rugs with ease, while its spinning mop pads do a good job on hard floors and automatically detach when vacuuming carpet. Other highlights include quiet mop washing and drying along with a slim design that can fit under low furniture.\n[Product: Roborock Qrevo Curv 2 Flow | https://www.amazon.com/roborock-Qrevo-Curv-Flow-Self-Cleaning/dp/B0FXG2BDTJ?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Roborock S8 MaxV Ultra | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D9B9LK9F/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.roborock.com%2Fproducts%2Froborock-s8-max-ultra-with-refill-drainage-system%3Fvariant%3D40697726828662%26country%3DUS%26currency%3DUSD%26utm_medium%3Dproduct_sync%26utm_source%3Dgoogle%26utm_content%3Dsag_organic%26utm_campaign%3Dsag_organic%26utm_source%3Dgoogle%26utm_medium%3Dcpc%26utm_campaign%3D21508780929%26utm_content%3Dx%26gad_source%3D1%26gad_campaignid%3D21518970394%26gbraid%3D0AAAAA-CrYEztb1LhcBELmkys2NY_LnjXt%26gclid%3DCj0KCQjwxvjRBhC2ARIsAI7KJa23ZE0tQ6zeY3nF5hsK1PZnRf4alHqO8dnT0zG4Nx0RYB3XczuRGlcaAu7uEALw_wcB]\n* You can pick up the Dreame X60 Max Ultra’s predecessor, the Dreame X50 Ultra, for $884.99 ($265 off) at Amazon and $807.99 at Dreame ($342). While its 20,000Pa suction isn’t quite as powerful as the X60 Ultra’s and it can’t tackle especially high thresholds as well, it’s still an excellent robot vacuum-mop hybrid. Its edge cleaning also isn’t quite as effective as the X60 Ultra’s, but you’re otherwise getting many of the same features for a lot less.\n* Dreame’s L40 Ultra Gen 2&nbsp;is on sale for $384.99 ($265 off) at Amazon and directly from Dreame with code L40UGWS. It delivers powerful 25,000Pa suction, AI-powered obstacle avoidance, and a self-cleaning dock that empties the dustbin, washes the mop, and refills its water tanks. Unlike the X50 Ultra, however, it lacks the ability to climb high thresholds or stairs.\n[Product: Narwal Flow 2 | https://www.amazon.com/NARWAL-Self-Cleaning-Recognition-Self-Emptying-Tangle-Free/dp/B0GFW4J291?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://narwalus.pxf.io/c/482924/2788060/31973?u=https%3A%2F%2Fus.narwal.com%2Fproducts%2Fnarwal-flow-2-robot-vacuum-and-mop]\n* The original Narwal Flow is available for $649.99 ($500 off) at Amazon, which is its best price to date. Like the Flow 2, it offers a self-cleaning roller mop along with a dock that automatically empties the dustbin and washes the mop and a tangle-resistant brush. The tradeoff is that it lacks the Flow 2’s upgraded AI-powered obstacle avoidance, uses lower-temperature water when washing the mop, and delivers slightly less suction power.\n* You can buy the SwitchBot K11 Plus on sale for around $169.99 at Amazon when you apply the on-page coupon, which is a new low price. It’s also available for $19 more from SwitchBot with code PDDAY53. It’s a tiny bot with an equally small self-emptying dock, making it a great fit for smaller spaces. Its suction power tops out at 6,000Pa, but it’s still an effective cleaning machine with a rubber roller brush and a single side brush that does a solid job picking up dirt, dust, and debris from both hard floors and carpets.\n[Product: Ecovacs Deebot X12 OmniCyclone | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GL7K63NV?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fecovacs-robotics-deebot-x12-omnicyclone-robot-vacuum-and-mop-22000pa-blast-suction-focusjet-self-washing-roller-mop-bagless-station-silver%2FJ3R855QVG8, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.ecovacs.com/us/deebot-robotic-vacuum-cleaner/deebot-x12-omnicyclone]\n[Product: Ecovacs Deebot X9 Pro Omni | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DZXFNVQ2/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fecovacs-robotics-deebot-x9-pro-omni-robot-vacuum-mop-real-time-self-washing-mopping-blast-16600pa-suction-triple-auto-mop-lift-black%2FJ3R8442FWT, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.ecovacs.com/us/deebot-robotic-vacuum-cleaner/deebot-x9-pro-omni/]\n* The Dreame L10s Pro Ultra is down to $349.99 when you buy it at Amazon, matching its best price to date and $950 less than its original launch price in 2024. Despite its age, it still offers a self-cleaning dock that can wash and dry its mop pads, dispense cleaning solution, refill its water tank, and empty its dustbin. It also features AI-powered obstacle avoidance. Its 7,000Pa suction is lower than Dreame’s newer models, and it can’t climb tall thresholds, but it’s still a lot of robot vacuum for the price.\n* The Shark Navigator Robot Vacuum RV2110 has dropped to $179 ($121 off) at Amazon. While we’ve previously seen it go for as low as $129.99, that’s still a notable 40 percent discount on the basic bot. The Navigator uses lidar-based navigation to create a map of your home and is equipped with a brushroll designed to minimize hair tangles.\nUpdate, June 26th: Adjusted prices and availability and added a deal for the Roborock S8 MaxV Ultra.",
