      "id": "theverge-2026-06-25-the-124-best-tech-deals-for-day-three-of-prime-day",
      "title": "The 124 best tech deals for day three of Prime Day",
      "summary": "It’s day three of Prime Day, folks. We’re nearly 75 percent of the way through Amazon’s four-day sales event, and unsurprisingly, many deals are still sticking around. There have been all kinds of discounts on things like TVs, smart home gadgets, chargers, headphones, and more.\nPrime Day typically isn’t as big of a deal as Black Friday, but it’s a chance to get some solid discounts on tech purchas",
      "body": "It’s day three of Prime Day, folks. We’re nearly 75 percent of the way through Amazon’s four-day sales event, and unsurprisingly, many deals are still sticking around. There have been all kinds of discounts on things like TVs, smart home gadgets, chargers, headphones, and more.\nPrime Day typically isn’t as big of a deal as Black Friday, but it’s a chance to get some solid discounts on tech purchases both large and small. Many items are at or near their all-time low prices, and in the case of things that got more expensive this year due to RAMageddon it can be a chance to nab them at their old prices.\nBe sure to check out all our coverage, which we are thoroughly checking and updating throughout all four days of Prime Day. But no roundup gets the same care and attention as our main roundup you see here. Our whole team pitches in on this one, so it’s our most varied, wide-ranging, and largest collection of deals. If you see it in any of our coverage, you know it’s something we’ve tested or owned and feel comfortable recommending.\nLegend of Zelda Tears of the Kingdom Switch 2 Edition\nSamsung P9 microSD Express Card\nHoto 3.6V Electric Screwdriver Kit Pro\n[Product: Echo Show 8 (2025) | https://www.amazon.com/Amazon-Echo-Show-8-Vibrant-HD-8.7-display-Graphite-Amazon/dp/B0DC8ZMR1P/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Famazon-echo-show-8-newest-model-vibrant-hd-8-7-display-with-spatial-audio-designed-for-alexa-graphite%2FJ39TLSRKP2, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Famazon-echo-show-8-2025%2F-%2FA-95002749]\n* Amazon’s Echo Show 11 is on sale for $149.99 ($80 off) at Amazon, which marks its best price to date. It’s almost identical to the Echo Show 8, except that it offers a larger and sharper 1080p resolution.\n* You can buy the latest&nbsp;Echo Show 5 for $59.99 ($30 off) at Amazon, which is one of its better prices in recent months though $20 shy of its all-time low. The smart display also works with Alexa Plus, but it’s smaller than the Echo Show 8 with less robust sound, and better suited for small table tops or office desks.\n[Product: Philips Hue smart bulb starter kit | https://www.amazon.com/Philips-Hue-Starter-Compatible-Assistant/dp/B096YFWVVS/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The Philips Hue Go Smart Portable Table Lamp is on sale for $123.47 ($53 off) at Amazon, which is a new low. The water resistant lamp can display millions of colors and lasts 48 hours on a single charge. It also offers customizable lighting effects and support for Matter, so you can control it via any major smart home platform.\n* If you like the idea of the Philips Hue portable smart lamp but want something cheaper, Govee’s Table Lamp Classic is down to a new low of $55.99 ($25 off) at Amazon. The rechargeable lamp isn’t weather-resistant, but it offers up to 30 hours of battery life, adjustable color temperatures, and dozens of preset scenes and colorful lighting effects.\n[Product: Philips Hue Twilight sleep-wake lamp | https://www.amazon.com/Philips-Hue-Bluetooth-Compatible-Assistant/dp/B0DBXHCZFG?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.philips-hue.com%2Fen-us%2Fp%2Fsleep-and-wake-up-light-twilight-sleep-and-wake-up-light-black%2F046677585631%3Forigin%3D_cmp%3D20961164112_kwd%3D%26gclsrc%3Daw.ds%26gad_source%3D1%26gad_campaignid%3D20967583196%26gbraid%3D0AAAAAqwUBEQcnFUTeIcjO4TDNO6aIyhRu%26gclid%3DCj0KCQjw_rPGBhCbARIsABjq9cewKhIjvdj0Yuk2L3FQU3p5wulNDSM8QvGpKyMBhUxuBcEq1KgSIwYaAsVWEALw_wcB]\n[Product: Amazon Echo Spot | https://www.amazon.com/All-new-Amazon-Echo-Spot-2024-release-Smart-alarm-clock-with-vibrant-sound-Alexa-Black/dp/B0BFC7WQ6R?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The foundation of a good smart home is Wi-Fi, so if you’re still rocking a router with Wi-Fi 6 or even 5, Prime Day is a good time to upgrade. All of Amazon’s eero mesh Wifi routers are on sale, and its flagship eero Wifi 7 Pro is down to $549.99 from $699.99. If you don’t need that much power, the equally capable eero Wifi 6E is down to $329.99 for a three-pack.\n[Product: Ring Battery Doorbell Plus (second-gen) | https://www.amazon.com/Ring-Battery-Doorbell-newest-Nickel/dp/B0GGLS1C4W?ref=amzdv_tplus_dp_dsk_bdldp_B0F14N7HHH_B0GGLS1C4W&tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Google Nest Wifi Pro | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BCQSYPZB?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The rubbed-bronze version of the versatile Yale Assure Lock 2 with WiFi is $70 off on Prime Day, discounted to $189.98. This lock features a real keypad, not a touchscreen, along with support for all the major smart home platforms, including Apple Home (although it doesn’t work with Home Key).\n[Product: Blink Video Doorbell (second-gen) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DGQZ8JZK?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Skylight Calendar 2 | https://www.amazon.com/Skylight-Calendar-Touchscreen-Wirecutter-Interactive/dp/B0G615HBG7/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fskylight-calendar-2-15-inch-touchscreen-smart-calendar-and-chore-chart-white%2FJ3R845QLVJ%2Fsku%2F6665550]\n* The Aura Carver is on sale for $143 ($36 off) at Amazon, which is its best price to date. The 10-inch Wi-Fi digital picture frame lets you add photos remotely through the Aura app, email, or supported cloud services. You also upload 30-second videos and live photos, all without requiring a subscription.\n[Product: Aqara Smart Lock U400 | https://www.amazon.com/Aqara-Fingerprint-Touchscreen-Rechargeable-Assistant/dp/B0FRS6T6HL/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: SwitchBot Bot | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07B7NXV4R?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.switch-bot.com%2Fproducts%2Fswitchbot-bot]\n[Product: SwitchBot Standing Circulator Fan | https://www.amazon.com/SwitchBot-Pedestal-Rechargeable-Oscillating-Adjustable/dp/B0FWC41M2P/ref=sr_1_2?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.switch-bot.com%2Fproducts%2Fswitchbot-standing-circulator-fan]\n[Product: Kindle Paperwhite (12th-gen) | http://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CFPJYX7P?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DDZJS3SB?tag=theverge02-20]\n* Amazon’s Kindle Colorsoft Signature Edition (its moniker for the 32GB version that supports wireless charging and has an auto-adjusting front light) is down to its best-ever price when purchased as a bundle. The “Essentials Bundle” that includes the e-reader, a leather cover, and a wireless charging dock is $257.97 ($132 off) at Amazon. The 16GB version that lacks the Signature features but includes the leather cover is $182.97 at Amazon. Read our review.\n* The other color e-reader that Amazon sells, the Scribe Colorsoft, is available in a bundle that’s steeply discounted. The 32GB model that includes a pen, leather folio, and a power adapter is $549.97 ($220 off) at Amazon, down from its usual sale price of $729.97. It’s a fantastic deal considering just the tablet and pen typically sell for $629.99 and hasn’t previously been discounted. Read our review.\n[Product: Kindle (11th-gen) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CNV9F72P?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DDZQTYHL?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Kobo Libra Colour | https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.kobobooks.com%2Fproducts%2Fkobo-libra-colour, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Fkobo-libra-colour-7-32gb-ereader-glare-free-colour-e-ink-kaleido-3-display-dark-mode-option-audiobooks-waterproof%2F-%2FA-91830243]\n[Product: Sony WH-1000XM6 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F3PQHWTZ?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsony-wh-1000xm6-best-wireless-noise-canceling-headphones-silver%2FJ7XSRH5R2X, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Fsony-wireless-noise-canceling-headphones%2F-%2FA-94760871%3Fpreselect%3D94649373]\n* Sony’s last-gen WH-1000XM5 noise-canceling headphones are selling for $198 at Amazon, which is the retailer’s best price yet. The set debuted for $399.99 and only really started dropping in price when its successor was released. While the XM6 gets the edge in terms of sound quality, comfort, and for having a foldable design, the XM5 are still fantastic — arguably the best over-ear headphones you can get at this price.\n[Product: AirPods Max 2 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GSS4SGZR?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FAirPods-Max-2-Blue%2F19864722287]\n[Product: Bose QuietComfort Ultra Earbuds (2nd Gen) | https://www.amazon.com/Bose-New-QuietComfort-Ultra-Earbuds/dp/B0F7M3HPBD?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fbose-quietcomfort-ultra-2nd-gen-true-wireless-noise-cancelling-in-ear-earbuds-black%2FJ7C5V6WCKZ]\n* The second-gen Bose QuietComfort Ultra over-ear headphones are selling for $379, one of their best prices yet, at Amazon. Originally $449, the noise-canceling headphones boast improved battery life with ANC switched on (up to 30 hours per charge), plus the ability to play lossless audio via their USB-C port, just like the AirPods Max 2.\n[Product: Pixel Buds 2a | https://www.amazon.com/Google-Pixel-Buds-Cancellation-Transparency/dp/B0FGKTDTRB/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://store.google.com/product/pixel_buds_2a?hl=en-US, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgoogle-pixel-buds-2a-wireless-earbuds-with-active-noise-cancellation-bluetooth-headphones-hazel%2FJ39TC8J6Z8%2Fsku%2F6642707]\n* JBL might not be the first brand you associate with great over-ear noise-canceling headphones, but its Tour One M3 Smart Tx are a sleeper hit that’s currently down to its best price yet at Amazon. You can grab them for $249.95, which is $200 off their original price. They’re comfortable, and they sound great. But what sets them apart from competitors is the Auracast-compatible audio transmitter that lets the headphones connect to (and share) audio with other Auracast devices.\n[Product: AirPods Pro 3 | https://www.amazon.com/Apple-Cancellation-Translation-Headphones-High-Fidelity/dp/B0FQFB8FMG?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FAirPods-nbsp-Pro-nbsp-3%2F17835006350, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fapple-airpods-pro-3-wireless-active-noise-cancelling-earbuds-with-heart-rate-sensing-feature-white%2FJJGCQLYK5F]\n[Product: Nothing Ear (a) | https://www.amazon.com/Nothing-Ear-Integration-Cancelling-Equaliser/dp/B0CXPRP216/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Nothing-Ear-Integration-Cancelling-Equaliser/dp/B0CXPRHTNB/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Nothing-Ear-Integration-Cancelling-Equaliser/dp/B0CXPRHTNB/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Shokz OpenRun Pro 2 | https://www.amazon.com/SHOKZ-New-OpenRun-Pro-Comfortable/dp/B0GGBQPG9C/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fshokz-openrun-pro-2-bone-conduction-sports-headphones-black%2FJ3GW298S85, https://shokzsingaporepteltd.pxf.io/c/482924/2826546/32610?u=https%3A%2F%2Fshokz.com%2Fproducts%2Fopenrunpro2]\n[Product: Shokz OpenFit 2 Plus | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fshokz-openfit-2-open-ear-true-wireless-bluetooth-earbuds-stone-blue%2FJ3GWSKCFCW, https://shokzsingaporepteltd.pxf.io/c/482924/2826546/32610?u=https%3A%2F%2Fshokz.com%2Fproducts%2Fopenfit2plus]\n[Product: Anker Laptop Power Bank | https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0DCBB2YTR?tag=theverge02-20, https://anker.pxf.io/c/482924/1543964/18023?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.anker.com%2Fproducts%2Fa1695-anker-power-bank-25000mah-165w, https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=nOD/rLJHOac&mid=44583&murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newegg.com%2Fp%2F39G-000T-00182]\n[Product: Apple MagSafe Charger (2m) | https://www.amazon.com/Apple-MagSafe-Charger-Fast-Charging-Capability/dp/B0FQFTXT7K/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Belkin BoostCharge Pro 3-in-1 Wireless Charging Stand with Qi2 15W | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DL86NC5Z/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DL8CK73P/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Belkin Charging Case for Nintendo Switch 2 | https://www.amazon.com/Belkin-Nintendo-Integrated-Protective-Cartridges/dp/B0FBQCJGL7/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The Apple Watch Series 11 has dropped to $279 in the 42mm GPS configuration (originally $399) at Amazon and Walmart, which is $20 lower than it has previously sold for. $299 has been the normal sale price for the past few months, but those patiently waiting for another price drop have been rewarded. If you want the larger 46mm GPS model, that’s down to $309 at Amazon and Walmart, which is another new low. Given it’s the latest model, it will support watchOS 27 as well as at least a few major software updates to come. Read our review.\n[Product: Apple Watch SE 3 | https://www.amazon.com/Apple-Smartwatch-Starlight-Aluminum-Always/dp/B0FQFW7M9H/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Apple-Smartwatch-Starlight-Aluminum-Always/dp/B0FQFJ2WRG/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* You can buy the Apple Watch Ultra 3 with an Ocean Band, Trail Loop strap, and Alpine Loop strap for $649 ($150 off) at Amazon, which is a new low price. The Ultra 3 is Apple’s most rugged and feature-packed smartwatch, making it a great choice for athletes and outdoorsy folks. It delivers up to 42 hours of battery life — six hours more than its predecessor — and features a larger wide-angle OLED display with a refresh rate that goes down to just 1Hz for battery savings, plus slimmer bezels. It also supports both satellite connectivity and 5G. Read our review.\n* Google’s Pixel Watch 4 has gotten discounts in both 41mm and 45mm sizes, whether you want the basic Wi-Fi/GPS feature offering, or you want to upgrade to the model that supports LTE. Originally $349.99, the 41mm GPS model is $289.99 at Amazon, while the 45mm version is $319.99. The LTE versions are $334.99 ($115 off) and $399.99 ($100 off). The Pixel Watch 4 is the best smartwatch for Android users (perhaps until the leaked Pixel Watch 5 launches), particularly for those who use a Pixel phone. Read our review.\n[Product: Fitbit Ace LTE | https://www.amazon.com/Fitbit-Google-Ace-LTE-Activity-Based/dp/B0CV5T2YG6?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://store.google.com/us/product/fitbit_ace_lte?hl=en-US, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Ffitbit-ace-lte-kids-smartwatch-with-in-app-calling-messaging-gps-mild-2024%2FJ39TC87JYC]\n* For Android smartwatch options that costs less, and are really only useful for Samsung phone owners, the Galaxy Watch 8 and Watch 8 Classic are discounted to $218.49 and $334.99, respectively. These are savings of $130 at minimum. Read our review.\n[Product: Oura Ring 4 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D9WV1TPJ/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fsite%2Fring-4-smart-ring-size-before-you-buy-with-oura-ring-4-sizing-kit-size-8-silver-2024%2F6595517.p%3FskuId%3D6595517, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fouraring.com%2Fproduct%2Frings%2Foura-ring-4%2Fsilver]\n[Product: Nex Playground | https://www.amazon.com/Playground-AI-Powered-Transforms-Not-Machine-Specific/dp/B0D2JGYX3F?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FNex-Playground-Game-System%2F9402952208, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fplayground-the-active-play-system-for-kids-families-indoor-physical-play-meets-interactive-family-fun%2FJ3Q5RY2VVT]\n* OLED gaming monitors that offer super-fast refresh rates are cheaper than usual during Prime Day, and several of them are from Asus. The company’s Strix XG27ACDNG 26.5-inch 1440p QD-OLED with a 360Hz refresh rate is down to $534 at Amazon. Its previous best price was $599.99, and it didn’t come around often. The next step up is the Swift PG27AQDP WOLED 1440p monitor with 480Hz refresh rate. It costs $664 during Prime Day at Amazon, down from around $800. Finally, the Asus ROG Swift PG27UCDM, a 4K QD-OLED with a 240Hz refresh rate, is $934 at Amazon — its best price yet that’s $265 off its original price.\n[Product: PlayStation Pulse Explore | https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FPlayStation-PULSE-Explore-Wireless-Earbuds%2F5113283042]\n[Product: Meta Quest 3S | https://www.amazon.com/Meta-Quest-128GB-Cardboard-Exclusive-Oculus/dp/B0F2GYMC8H?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fsite%2Fquest-3s-128gb-dive-into-mixed-reality-get-a-3-month-trial-of-meta-horizon-included-white%2F6622623.p%3FskuId%3D6622623]\n[Product: Legend of Zelda Tears of the Kingdom Switch 2 Edition | https://www.amazon.com/Legend-ZeldaTM-Kingdom-Nintendo-SwitchTM-Switch/dp/B0BX854JYZ?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Fthe-legend-of-zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-nintendo-switch-2-edition%2F-%2FA-94694197]\n* Metroid Prime 4: Beyond for the Nintendo Switch 2 is down to $44.99 in physical cartridge format at Amazon, down from $69.99. It’s the biggest deal we’ve seen yet for the Switch 2 version of the game. Previously, we’d seen $40 deals for the original Switch version, but to unlock faster loading and better graphics, Switch 2 owners would have to pay $10 for the upgrade pack.\n[Product: Resident Evil Requiem | https://www.amazon.com/Resident-Evil-Requiem-Amazon-Exclusive-PlayStation/dp/B0FY929QN1?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Resident-Evil-Requiem-Amazon-Exclusive-Nintendo/dp/B0FY9YW365?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Resident-Evil-Requiem-Amazon-Exclusive-Xbox/dp/B0FY9BBRJS?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Metal Gear Solid Delta: Snake Eater | https://www.amazon.com/METAL-GEAR-SOLID-TACTICAL-PlayStation-5/dp/B0D4RJGFDT?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/METAL-GEAR-SOLID-TACTICAL-PlayStation-5/dp/B0D4SDQCG3?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FMetal-Gear-Solid-Snake-Eater-Tactical-Edition-PlayStation-5%2F6383222967]\n[Product: Gigabyte 27-inch 1440p W-OLED gaming monitor | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GKF8K19Q?th=1&tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Acer Predator 26.5-inch 1440p QD-OLED gaming monitor | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G5Z5N274?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Samsung P9 microSD Express Card | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FT99KCV8?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FT995SPF?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: EasySMX S10 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FM7Z4D7D/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgo.skimresources.com%3Fid%3D1025X1701640%26xs%3D1%26url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fwww.easysmx.com%252Fproducts%252Feasysmx-s10-gaming-controller-for-switch-2-tmr-sticks-hd-rumble-motion-control, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FM7WDJ4H/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Lego Star Wars Imperial Star Destroyer | https://www.amazon.com/LEGO-Destroyer-Buildable-Anniversary-Minifigure/dp/B0CRWRY5RM?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The Lego Star Wars: The Clone Wars Coruscant Guard Gunship has dropped to $97.99 ($42 off) at Amazon, which is its best price of the year and only $2 more than its all-time low. The 1,083-piece building set comes with five minifigures, including the likes of Chancellor Palpatine and Padmé Amidala, along with features like dual pilot cockpits, stud shooters, adjustable cannons, and an opening cabin with space for troops and gear.\n* You can buy the Lego Robot World Roller-Coaster Park on sale for $69.99 ($30 off) at Amazon, which matches its best price to date. The 986-piece set comes with everything you need to build a robot-themed roller coaster, including eight mini-figures, a detachable mech action figure, and accessories like toy cell phones.\n[Product: Lego Piranha Plant | https://www.amazon.com/LEGO-TBD-Super-Mario-71426/dp/B0BXQ3M8JH/?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Flego-super-mario-piranha-plant-building-set-71426%2F-%2FA-87830626]\n* The Lego Wild Animals: Majestic Rhino with Birds set is down to $41.99 ($18 off) at Amazon, which also matches its record low price. The 780-piece set lets you build one of three posable animals from the African savannah— a rhino with colorful birds, a hippo, or a walrus — and includes accessories like fish for the walrus display.\n* If you’d rather not be tied to a specific build, the 790-piece Lego Classic Large Creative Brick Box is on sale for $33.49 ($26 off) at Amazon, which is $10 shy of its all-time low and one of the better prices we’ve seen this year. It comes with bricks in 33 colors, along with windows, doors, wheels, and baseplates, so you can build everything from houses and vehicles to animals.\n[Product: Lego Botanicals Flower Bouquet Building Set | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08HW1L75J?tag=theverge02-20]\n* If you prefer something a little simpler (or cheaper), the Lego Roses set includes 120 pieces to build two red roses with adjustable stems, and we often recommend it as a sweet gift for a partner, friend, or family member. It’s on sale for $8.79 ($7 off) at Amazon and Target, which is $2 shy of its best price to date.\n* Lego’s Lotus Flowers set is another budget-friendly build, and it’s nearly half off at $7.99&nbsp;($7 off) at Amazon, which is its best price of the year. The 220-piece set includes two blooming lotus flowers and a budding flower with pink-and-white petals and long green stems.\nRobot vacuum and mop deals\n[Product: Roborock Saros 20 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G64XBNWY?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.roborock.com%2Fproducts%2Froborock-saros-20]\n[Product: Eufy Omni C28 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FWK41WF2?tag=theverge02-20, https://eufy-us.sjv.io/c/482924/999452/13094?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eufy.com%2Fproducts%2Ft211a110%3Fvariant%3D45573047124154]\n* The Roborock Q10 S5 Plus is down to $264.99 ($285 off) at Amazon, which matches its lowest price to date. The Q10 S5 Plus is one of our favorite budget-friendly robot vacuum / mop hybrids, combining good AI-powered obstacle avoidance with automatic carpet detection. It also features a vibrating mop that does a solid job scrubbing hard floors while lifting itself over rugs, and the set includes a self-emptying dock for added convenience. It can’t match the suction power or tall threshold-climbing abilities of pricier models like the Saros 20, but this is a good value under $300.\n[Product: Narwal Flow 2 | https://www.amazon.com/NARWAL-Self-Cleaning-Recognition-Self-Emptying-Tangle-Free/dp/B0GFW4J291?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://narwalus.pxf.io/c/482924/2788060/31973?u=https%3A%2F%2Fus.narwal.com%2Fproducts%2Fnarwal-flow-2-robot-vacuum-and-mop]\n* Dreame’s X60 Max Ultra is on sale for $1,344.99 ($355 off) at Amazon, which is its best price to date. We highly recommend the Dreame X60 Ultra for homes with lots of carpet, as it combines powerful 35,000Pa suction with dual rubber brushes that excel at lifting hair and debris. It can also climb over tall thresholds and thick rugs with ease, while its spinning mop pads do a good job on hard floors and automatically detach when vacuuming carpet. Other highlights include quiet mop washing and drying along with a slim design that can fit under low furniture.\n[Product: Roborock Qrevo Curv 2 Flow | https://www.amazon.com/roborock-Qrevo-Curv-Flow-Self-Cleaning/dp/B0FXG2BDTJ?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Froborock-qrevo-curv-2-flow-robot-vacuum-and-mop-white%2FJJ8F5PCTK2%2Fsku%2F6668432, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.roborock.com%2Fproducts%2Froborock-qrevo-curv-2-flow]\n* Dreame’s L40 Ultra Gen 2&nbsp;is on sale for $384.99 ($265 off) at Amazon and directly from Dreame (with code L40UGWS). It delivers powerful 25,000Pa suction, AI-powered obstacle avoidance, and a self-cleaning dock that empties the dustbin, washes the mop, and refills its water tanks. Unlike the X50 Ultra, however, it lacks the ability to climb high thresholds or stairs.\n[Product: Ecovacs Deebot X12 OmniCyclone | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GL7K63NV?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fecovacs-robotics-deebot-x12-omnicyclone-robot-vacuum-and-mop-22000pa-blast-suction-focusjet-self-washing-roller-mop-bagless-station-silver%2FJ3R855QVG8, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.ecovacs.com/us/deebot-robotic-vacuum-cleaner/deebot-x12-omnicyclone]\n* You can buy the SwitchBot K11 Plus on sale for a new all-time low of $169.99 ($230 off) at Amazon (when you click the $20 on-page coupon) or $188 directly from SwitchBot with code PDDAY53. It’s a tiny bot with an equally small self-emptying dock, making it a great fit for smaller spaces. Its suction power tops out at 6,000Pa, but it’s still an effective cleaning machine with a rubber roller brush and a single side brush that does a solid job picking up dirt, dust, and debris from both hard floors and carpets.\n[Product: Dyson PencilWash | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GKJ1PYJZ/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Google Pixel 10A | http://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GHRHXVN1?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgoogle-pixel-10a-128gb-unlocked-lavender%2FJ39TC8CKZ8%3FskuId%3D6668561, https://www.amazon.com/Google-Pixel-10a-Smartphone-Detection/dp/B0GHRHNCZQ/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Google Pixel 10 Pro | https://www.amazon.com/Google-Pixel-Pro-Smartphone-Fast-Charging/dp/B0FFTT2J6N/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://store.google.com/us/product/pixel_10_pro, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgoogle-pixel-10-pro-128gb-unlocked-obsidian%2FJ39TC8J8GF]\n* The Nothing 4A Pro with 12GB of RAM and 256GB of storage is down to $509.99 at Amazon, Walmart, and directly from Nothing, a hearty discount from its original $599 price. It’s the biggest, most high-end phone you can get for around this price, if you don’t want to settle for the Pixel 10A. Its 6.83-inch screen has a 144Hz refresh rate, but really what sets this one apart is its unique design. The Glyph Matrix display on its rear that can show the time or show an icon to alert you of notifications. Read our review.\n[Product: Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G4SX79VJ/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsamsung-galaxy-s26-ultra-256gb-unlocked-black%2FJJGRF36YGZ%2Fsku%2F6669733, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G4SWN34T/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Google Pixel Pro 10 Fold | https://www.amazon.com/Google-Pixel-Pro-Fold-Smartphone/dp/B0FFTNCY4Z/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://store.google.com/config/pixel_10_pro_fold?, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgoogle-pixel-10-pro-fold-256gb-unlocked-moonstone%2FJ39TC8JXSY]\n4K TV and monitor deals\n[Product: LG C5 OLED TV | https://www.amazon.com/LG-Upscaling-Filmmaker-Orchestra-OLED65C5PUA/dp/B0DYQM4BDB?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Flg-55-class-c5-series-oled-evo-ai-4k-uhd-smart-webos-tv-2025%2FJJ8VPZTR8R, https://www.amazon.com/LG-Upscaling-Filmmaker-Orchestra-OLED65C5PUA/dp/B0DYQF1Q3Z?tag=theverge02-20]\n* 55 inches is a good size for TVs, and getting one as good as the TCL QM6K for only $447.99 ($50 off) at Amazon is worth it. It’s particularly good for someone looking for a lower-priced gaming TV, as it supports high refresh rates up to 4K/144Hz with a PC (or 1080p at 288Hz) with VRR and has low input lag. It’s not the light cannon that more expensive TCL TVs are, but in a light-controlled room there’s enough brightness for watching or playing anything.\n* The 65-inch Hisense Canvas TV is on sale for $849.99 at Amazon, which is a new low price for the 2026 model. The Hisense CanvasTV is an excellent budget-friendly alternative to Samsung’s The Frame, one that comes with a free magnetic bezel, access to over 1,000 artworks, and runs on the excellent Google TV interface.\n[Product: Samsung S90F | https://www.amazon.com/Samsung-55-Inch-Processor-Upscaling-Xcelerator/dp/B0DXN7PBFC?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Samsung-55-Inch-Processor-Upscaling-Xcelerator/dp/B0DXMJGQWC?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/Samsung-55-Inch-Processor-Upscaling-Xcelerator/dp/B0DXN1QNFW?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The 32-inch Asus ProArt 6K display is $999.99 at Amazon during Prime Day, down from its original list price of $1,299. The IPS monitor can display up to 6,016 x 3,384 resolution, and it covers 98 percent of the DCI-P3 gamut and 100 percent of the sRGB gamut. It features HDMI 2.1, DisplayPort 1.4, plus two Thunderbolt 4 ports that can deliver up to 96W of power for laptops and be used to daisychain with other monitors.\n* A smaller 27-inch 5K ProArt display from Asus is down to $634 at Amazon (usually priced around $780), marking its best price yet. The PA27JCV seems like a solid alternative if Apple’s Studio Display or other options are a little too pricey. The ProArt monitor features a built-in KVM switch, HDR support, and a bevy of connectivity options, including HDMI, DisplayPort, and USB-C (with up to 96W charging).\n[Product: TCL QM8K Series QD-Mini LED TV | https://www.amazon.com/TCL-75QM8K-120HZ-144HZ-Reflective-Television/dp/B0F53HDFBR/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FTCL-98QM8K-TV%2F15982572337, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Ftcl-75-class-qm8k-series-4k-uhd-hdr-qd-mini-led-smart-tv-with-google-tv-2025%2FJ36QYTQZ3P]\n* Dell makes a 27-inch 4K monitor with USB-C video-out, and it’s selling for just $251.72 (originally $349.99) at Amazon. Beyond being a good pick for easy connectivity with a Mac, or a Windows machine that supports USB-C video, the display has solid specs, like a 120Hz refresh rate, AMD FreeSync Premium adaptive sync to prevent screen tearing, and USB-C charging up to 65W PD. A 1440p version with similar specs (but a faster 144Hz refresh rate) is just $199.99.\nHome theater and speaker deals\n[Product: Echo Dot Max | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D6SX8VLQ?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The WiiM Sound smart speaker (in black or white) that has a built-in circular display and supports multi-room pairing is down to $239.20 at Crutchfield from $299. The HomePod-esque speaker uses AI to adjust sound to fit your room, and it’s platform-agnostic, so it can work with practically any streaming service.\n[Product: Sonos Five | https://www.amazon.com/Sonos-Five-High-Fidelity-Speaker-Superior/dp/B087CC4QH4/?tag=theverge02-20, https://sonos.sjv.io/c/482924/2804767/32256?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sonos.com%2Fen-us%2Fshop%2Ffive%2F, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsonos-five-high-fidelity-wireless-speaker-black%2FJ3W5YWHQZK%2Fsku%2F6411135]\n* Hisense’s Dolby Atmos-ready 5.1.4 soundbar system is discounted during Prime Day. The AX5140Q costs $329.99 at Amazon, which is $70 off its original price. The 40-inch soundbar includes forward- and upward-firing speakers, a wireless subwoofer, plus two wireless satellite speakers that have their own forward- and upward-firing drivers. I wish I had gotten this set instead of the Vizio Elevate SE — it’s good, but this seems a lot better for the price. The soundbar features multiple ways to connect devices, including aux-in, optical-in, plus two HDMI inputs, one of which supports eARC.\n[Product: Sonos Era 100 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BW34LCB8/?tag=theverge02-20, https://sonos.sjv.io/c/482924/2804767/32256?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sonos.com%2Fen-us%2Fshop%2Fera-100, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsonos-era-100-wifi-and-bluetooth-smart-speaker-each-black%2FJ39H373RL3]\n* The Era 100 SL that lacks a microphone is $20 less, costing $159 at Amazon during Prime Day. If you don’t feel the desire to get chatty with your electronics, this is an easy way to save $20 on your next Sonos speaker.\n* Sony’s Bravia Theater Bar 9 soundbar is down to $998 at Amazon during Prime Day. It typically retails for $1,498, though it also typically sells at this very discount during other big shopping events, like Black Friday. The 43.3-inch soundbar packs a whopping 13 speakers, including a mix of forward-, side- and upward-firing speakers.\n[Product: Amazon Echo Studio (2025) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FBHDQ94L/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Bose TV Speaker | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B088KRPCQJ?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fbose-tv-speaker-bluetooth-soundbar-black%2FJ7C5V6RW57, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.bose.com/p/home-theater/bose-tv-speaker/TVSPKR-SOUNDBAR.html]\n* Bose’s Smart Ultra soundbar has dropped to $699, down from its original $999 price, at Amazon. To be transparent, this price was available ahead of Prime Day, so it’s not a brand-spankin’-new deal. However, it’s a good deal if you’re considering building out a Bose speaker ecosystem with a few of its Lifestyle Ultra wireless speakers that can extend the sound.\n[Product: Ultimate Ears Wonderboom 4 | https://www.amazon.com/Ultimate-Ears-WONDERBOOM-360-Degree-Waterproof/dp/B0BRXJ9WTD?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FUltimate-Ears-Wonderboom-4-EXC-Blue%2F13495423154, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fultimate-ears-wonderboom-4-portable-wireless-bluetooth-speaker-with-waterproof-dustproof-and-floatable-design-cobalt-blue%2FJ7H7ZYG2F7]\n[Product: Google TV Streamer (4K) | https://www.amazon.com/Google-TV-Streamer-Streaming-Entertainment/dp/B0D8WJYSF9/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://store.google.com/config/google_tv_streamer?hl=en-US, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgoogle-tv-streamer-4k-fast-streaming-device-in-4k-hdr-32-gb-of-storage-hazel%2FJ3GT5ZSHC5%2Fsku%2F6642280]\n* Amazon’s Fire TV Stick 4K Max is its highest-end streaming stick, and it costs $34.99 at Amazon. It’s a good price considering its relatively speedy performance, plus support for Dolby Vision and HDR10 Plus HDR formats, along with Dolby Atmos audio. It works with Wi-Fi 6E routers, too.\n* Most people looking for an affordable streaming stick should opt for the Fire TV Stick 4K Max, but if you want to save a little money and don’t mind slower performance (and fewer features), the Fire TV Stick 4K Select will get the job done. It’s down to $17.99 at Amazon, which is just $2 more than the model that tops out at 1080p resolution.\n[Product: Apple AirTags (second-generation) | https://www.amazon.com/Apple-AirTag-2nd-Generation-Precision/dp/B0GJTXVN9Z?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fapple-airtag-4-pack-2nd-generation-2026-white%2FJJGCQLTTF3, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.costco.com%2Fp%2F-%2Fapple-airtag-2nd-generation-4-pack-includes-additional-airtag-1-pack-2nd-generation%2F4000277035]\n[Product: Tile Slim (2024) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D637HK8Q?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FLife360-Tile-Slim-2024-1-Pack-Blk%2F6484423857, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DZPK6MW1?tag=theverge02-20]\n* Samsung’s 512GB T9 microSD card is $104.99 ($95 off MSRP) at Amazon. It’s not an Express card for the Nintendo Switch 2, but it’s an A2 V30 model with loads of storage for a DJI Osmo Pocket or similar creator cameras.\n[Product: Xreal One Pro | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fxreal-one-pro-ar-glasses-w-x1-chip-171-fhd-120hz-display-w-sound-by-bose-for-iphone16-15-steam-rog-mac-pc-android-ios-57-66mm-ipd%2FCZTVG22GYF%2Fsku%2F6637456%3Futm_source%3Dfeed%26extStoreId%3D104%26ref%3D212%26loc%3D20510845600%26gclsrc%3Daw.ds%26gad_source%3D1%26gad_campaignid%3D20510847514%26gbraid%3D0AAAAAD-ORIjRMSscJAZ-s9Xtg54_H8SFJ%26gclid%3DCj0KCQjwj47OBhCmARIsAF5wUEEWYHQjHiPgmA9wQpvtYSb2PD87FhEyY_9iHiRy75Yxyh4Nh1XLYiMaAn41EALw_wcB, https://xreal.pxf.io/c/482924/3225795/36319?u=https%3A%2F%2Fus.shop.xreal.com%2Fproducts%2Fxreal-one-pro]\n* The company’s Xreal 1S smart glasses are also discounted during Prime Day. You can pick up a pair for $399 (normally $449) at Amazon. While nearly identical in terms of design to the pricier One Pro (they also feature three degrees of freedom, letting you pin virtual content in place), their field of view and clarity aren’t as good. Additionally, their optics let in more light, so they aren’t as good of a pick unless you intend to view content mostly in dimly-lit spaces. Still, they’re comfortable, with great build quality, and they’re easy to use.\n[Product: Hoto 3.6V Electric Screwdriver Kit Pro | https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0BLMQ8BXB/ref=ewc_pr_img_1?smid=A2ZXT6R0FR7K6V&psc=1&tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Fanttik S1 Pro Cordless Electric Screwdriver | https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0C141QZVL/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Ffanttik.com%2Fproducts%2Ffanttik-nex-s1-pro-cordless-screwdriver, https://www.costco.com.au/Home-Improvement/Tools/Power-Tools/Fanttik-S1-Pro-Cordless-Electric-Screwdriver/p/1800313]\n* For an even more compact and affordable electric screwdriver, the standard Fanttik S1 is just $23.99 ($26 off) at Amazon in both gray and pink colors. The tiny handheld driver comes with five double-ended bits for most basic around-the-house projects.\n* The 11-inch M4-powered iPad Air is on sale for $519 ($79 off) at Amazon and Best Buy, which is its best price to date. The Air is a sizable step up from Apple’s entry-level iPad, combining a faster M4 chip with 12GB of RAM, Apple Intelligence features, and support for the Apple Pencil Pro. It also includes newer connectivity standards like Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6, making it more future-proof. Read our review.\n[Product: Cuisinart 8-in-1 1800W toaster oven | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09HSWBTN4?th=1&tag=theverge02-20]\n* Cricut’s Maker 4, a capable cutting machine that can make detailed cuts, draw, write, engrave, and more, is down to $379 during Prime Day at Amazon. It’s a big discount off its usual $449 price, and the best price we’ve seen since an early January discount.\n* For something simpler and smaller, the Cricut Joy 2 Essential Bundle includes the Joy 2 automatic cutting and drawing machine, plus numerous materials to get you started. It’s down to $109 (originally $139) at Amazon, the lowest price we’ve seen. The Ultimate Bundle with even more materials and tools is $146 (originally $209) at Amazon. Read our review.\n[Product: Ninja Creami Deluxe 11-in-1 Ice Cream Maker | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0B9CZ6XBQ?th=1&tag=theverge02-20]\n* Wearable lights from Glocusent that make it easier to read or do hobbies with your hands are always popular with Verge readers. The company’s bendable neck light that supports three color temperatures and six levels of brightness is down to $16.24 (originally $28.99) at Amazon. It’s not a big discount from its normal price of about $19, but it’s also not a lot of money for what might become a staple in your everyday carry setup. It’s rechargeable via USB-C, and can last up to 80 hours per charge.\n[Product: Birdbuddy Pro (solar) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DHY6B9GY?tag=theverge02-20, https://mybirdbuddy.com/product/smart-bird-feeder-pro-solar-v2/]\n* The days of multi-hundred-dollar discounts on MacBooks are behind us for now, but the base 14-inch MacBook Pro with an M5 chip for $1,549 ($150 off) at Amazon and Best Buy is still a solid deal. It’s powerful enough for the average content creator, comes with 16GB of RAM and 1TB of storage, and has lots of ports. Read our review.\n[Product: Apple MacBook Air (M5) | https://www.amazon.com/Apple-2026-MacBook-13-inch-Laptop/dp/B0GR1493ZV?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fapple-macbook-air-13-inch-laptop-m5-chip-with-10-core-cpu-and-8-core-gpu-16gb-memory-512gb-ssd-starlight%2FJJGCQLKCJZ, https://www.amazon.com/Apple-2026-MacBook-15-inch-Laptop/dp/B0GR1N82GJ/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* Moft has a variety of deals on its origami-style cases and stands. You can get its folding 2-in-1 Laptop Carry Sleeve, a sleek laptop case that doubles as a portable stand, for $51.96 ($13 off) at Amazon in four sizes and up to 11 different colors. Or, if you don’t mind some adhesive, the Moft Laptop Stand in select colors is $19.99 ($5 off) at Amazon. The super thin attachment sticks to the bottom of your laptop to give you a fold-out stand anywhere you go.\n[Product: 2025 Asus ROG Zephyrus G14 | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fasus-rog-zephyrus-g14-14-oled-3k-120hz-gaming-laptop-amd-ryzen-9-270-16gb-lpddr5x-geforce-rtx-5060-1tb-ssd-platinum-white%2FJJGGLH72GT, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fasus-rog-zephyrus-g14-14-3k-oled-120hz-gaming-laptop-copilot-pc-amd-ryzen-ai-9-hx-32gb-ram-nvidia-rtx-5080-2tb-platinum-white%2FJJGGLHXFWZ]",
