      "id": "techcrunch-2026-06-24-elon-suffers-another-day-short-of-trillionaire-status",
      "title": "Elon suffers another day short of trillionaire status",
      "summary": "Right now he's merely a several-hundred-billionaire, according to Bloomberg's Billionaires Index.",
      "body": "4:09 PM PDT · June 24, 2026\nImage Credits:Spencer Platt / Getty Images\nIn a world marred with oppression and strife, one injustice rises above all else: Elon Musk is not currently a trillionaire.\nWhen SpaceX went public earlier this month, Musk became the world’s first trillionaire. He declared in a victory lap-slash-speech that he aspires to take all of us to the moon, Mars, and “maybe beyond the solar system.” He awkwardly threw his fists in the air while his acolytes cheered him on.\nBut stock prices fluctuate, so right now he’s merely a several-hundred-billionaire, according to Bloomberg’s Billionaires Index.\nFrankly, it’s embarrassing. How will Musk support his legion of offspring? Can he even afford to keep expanding his already considerable brood, given his outspoken pronatalism? The math is getting complicated.\nWe wish him the best as he navigates this trying time. And, Elon, if you need a good rice and beans recipe, or some tips on how to win big at the thrift store, we can point you in the right direction.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Amanda Silberling",
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-24T23:09:39.000Z",
