    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-06-23-the-meta-quest-3s-is-on-sale-for-297-which-is-basically-its-",
      "title": "The Meta Quest 3S is on sale for $297 — which is basically its old price",
      "summary": "The Meta Quest 3S VR headset with 128GB of storage is $296.79 (about $53 off) at Amazon. This is Meta’s entry-level VR headset, which launched back in 2024 for $299.99 before getting a price increase this year to $349.99. So it’s not exactly the most exciting deal, but it’s about as good as you’re likely to find these days for a new unit.\nThe base model Quest blends a bit of the higher-end Quest 3",
      "body": "The Meta Quest 3S VR headset with 128GB of storage is $296.79 (about $53 off) at Amazon. This is Meta’s entry-level VR headset, which launched back in 2024 for $299.99 before getting a price increase this year to $349.99. So it’s not exactly the most exciting deal, but it’s about as good as you’re likely to find these days for a new unit.\nThe base model Quest blends a bit of the higher-end Quest 3 and older Quest 2 for a Goldilocks-style compromise. Like other Quests, it’s a standalone unit that operates wirelessly — until it’s time to charge it, of course. It plays a wide selection of games from the Quest store, like Batman: Arkham Shadow and Supernatural (once it relaunches), and if you don’t mind some added latency, you can wirelessly stream Steam games from your PC.\n[Product: Meta Quest 3S | https://www.amazon.com/Meta-Quest-128GB-Cardboard-Exclusive-Oculus/dp/B0F2GYMC8H?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fsite%2Fquest-3s-128gb-dive-into-mixed-reality-get-a-3-month-trial-of-meta-horizon-included-white%2F6622623.p%3FskuId%3D6622623]\nWhile the much pricier Quest 3 uses lighter, flatter pancake lenses for its optics, the 3S uses fresnel lenses just like the Quest 2 generation. But other than that, it’s got many similarities as the $600 Quest 3: the same Qualcomm Snapdragon XR2 Gen 2 processor, the same cameras with color passthrough video, and the same controllers. What you pay much more for in the Quest 3 is higher image quality, thanks in part to those refined optics and a higher resolution per eye. But the Quest 3S still looks fine with its 1832 x 1920 pixels per eye.\nIt’s a shame we’re no longer seeing the previous kinds of low prices the Quest 3S used to fall to, like when it was $249 around Black Friday, but with the way things are going this is as good as it gets for now.\nRead our review of the Meta Quest 3S",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Deals",
        "Gadgets",
        "Meta",
        "Prime Day",
        "Tech",
        "Verge Shopping",
        "Wearable"
      ],
      "author": "Antonio G. Di Benedetto",
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-23T21:00:00.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/25826092/257467_Meta_Quest_3S_AKrales_0140.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.732984293194,100,78.534031413613",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/954049/meta-quest-3s-vr-headset-prime-day-deal-sale",
